WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.279
The first is a commitment to appropriate
animal care.

2
00:00:03.279 --> 00:00:08.759
This framework prioritizes measurable
welfare and minimizing distress, rather than

3
00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:11.699
asserting strict biological equality
between humans and animals.

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.520
The second is a responsibility to the
public.

5
00:00:15.479 --> 00:00:18.580
Researchers must clearly communicate the
medical benefits derived from their work,

6
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.639
while calmly and truthfully addressing
societal concerns regarding animal welfare.

7
00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:26.100
The third is maintaining scientific and
medical integrity.

8
00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:31.500
This requires optimal protocol design,
exhaustive database searching to prevent

9
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.059
redundant experiments, and stringent
professional peer review.

10
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.660
This visualization of a perfectly balanced
scale represents the final responsibility,

11
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.479
the strict mathematical stewardship of
animal resources.

12
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.880
Proper stewardship demands selecting the exact right
model system and calculating the precise number

13
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.080
of subjects needed to achieve statistical
significance, using neither too

14
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.759
many, which causes unnecessary harm, nor

15
00:00:57.759 --> 00:01:00.079
too few, which renders the data useless.

16
00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:05.540
These four pillars take abstract moral
empathy and convert it into objective,

17
00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.820
enforceable standard operating procedures.
